comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T04:18:52.614Z","harness:codex","Design and duplicate check: reviewed all 262 open titles, all-status search, full sibling metadata, and closed alias/census foundations pm-0z7n and pm-yy8rmx. Group discovery and reconciliation under item duplicates (existing detector), item duplicates audit, and item duplicates merge. Place comment coverage under item audit-comments because it measures annotations rather than duplicate work. Extend the shared namespace mechanism to preserve complete nested handlers, SDK identities, flags, cursors, and compatibility hints. GitHub intake currently has zero open PRs/issues and zero open Dependabot/code-scanning alerts."
  "2026-09-10T04:25:10.842Z","harness:codex","TDD red: the new sandboxed namespace suite failed all 11 cases before implementation, covering seven legacy mappings, nested handler identity, copy addressing, direct package registration, and rejection of undeclared package grafts. The implementation now generalizes relocation to declared nested paths and keeps the existing handlers."
  "2026-09-10T06:17:56.786Z","harness:codex","Final verification: 660 test files and 8680 tests pass. Exact coverage is statements 63924/63924, branches 48623/48623, functions 13290/13290, lines 61268/61268. Source/export/member docstrings are 100 percent. TypeScript, ESLint, zero-clone jscpd, static structure, SDK/command/flag parity, refusal recovery, token budgets, graph composition, record integrity, credential scan, and linked tests passed. Manual temporary-project acceptance and packed npm/Bun/npx/bunx consumers passed. The independent public verifier confirms published 2026.9.9; this implementation is pending PR review and merge. GitHub currently has zero open PRs/issues and zero open dependency/code/secret alerts."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T06:06:48.274Z","harness:codex","Annotation coverage and duplicate reconciliation share the item noun but answer different questions. item audit-comments owns annotation completeness; item duplicates, item duplicates audit, and item duplicates merge own discovery and reconciliation. Existing root spellings remain permanent hidden aliases with bounded migration guidance."
